      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "+1 for this. I'd really love to be able to move my head around and nod and boop people on my linux machine.\n\nThe two solutions I can see are :\n\n- Make hands, head rotation, shoulders controllable via OSC instead of selfie expression directly acting on avatar. This would be the most \"open\" and useful change. It would also allow people (in a cross-platform way) to have custom alternatives to selfie expression, maybe more precise control, etc\n\n- Make VRChat able to stream a video input in a way that's linux/proton compatible, i.e. as @{67e7f5c1020588e99bfbad57|full_name} said accept video stream URLS, or change video capture implementation",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
